Original commit body from 6566b9f92ede1cb596ae7d07245f09bba347a516:

WI-bifob's own contract states exclusions are reported "on the CONFIRMED path
as well as the violated one". Only the confirmed path implemented it. On the
violated path excluded_flows was attached to the dataclass and never rendered,
and cli.py prints details alone -- so a text-mode reader of a violated claim
never learned that flows existed and were set aside by a policy they did not
choose. flow_origins (WI-vazal) reached no text surface at all, on either path.

Both are now spliced into details, which is where this module already keeps the
confirmed-path clause -- one home for the prose, not two.

MEASURED: 5 violated verdicts across the nine-repo cohort carry exclusions that
were previously invisible in text. caddy's untrusted-input-no-network alone was
silently setting aside 42 flows. And origins matters where it was measured: all
140 flows on pretix's largest violated claim are database-read-to-database-
write, which changes what a reader does about the claim.

SECOND HALF -- is_test_file stays broad and the bucket says WHICH rule fired
(owner ruling 2026-08-03). The predicate matches bench/, benches/, fixtures/,
testdata/, mocks/, fakes/, harnesses/, fv/, testutils/ and more. That breadth
is correct for its callers, but reporting all of it as test_sourced told the
reader something false about a benchmark directory. excluded_flows keys now
carry the reason: test_sourced, mock_sourced, fixture_sourced,
benchmark_sourced, test_support_sourced, plus the unchanged migration_sourced.

ONE CLASSIFIER, TWO CONSUMERS. paths.classify_test_file holds the rules and
returns the reason; is_test_file is now literally
`classify_test_file(path) is not None`. A separate categoriser beside the
boolean would drift from it on the first edit, and "when a production
classification exists for the thing you are counting, counting it yourself IS
the bug" (L53) is a lesson this codebase has already paid for five times. A
property test over a 46-path corpus asserts the two can never disagree, with a
non-vacuity floor so an all-True corpus cannot satisfy it trivially.

MEASURED, AND THE HONEST RESULT IS THAT THE SPLIT RECLASSIFIES NOTHING HERE.
Cohort-wide the excluded population is 692 flows before and after, still
{test_sourced: 675, migration_sourced: 17} -- every excluded flow in these nine
repos is genuine test code or a migration. That is conclusive for this cohort
rather than a sampling limit, since the bucket counts ARE the classification.
So this is insurance against a misleading label, not a correction of one that
was firing, and it is reported that way rather than as a win.

Zero verdicts move: 54 rows, 0 changed on (verdict, evidence_count, shown).

A production function named test_* is a footgun, found on the first run: pytest
collects any test_-prefixed symbol imported into a test module as a test case,
so the first draft failed with "fixture 'path' not found". Named
classify_test_file.

Envelope schema 1.4 -> 1.5. Not purely additive, deliberately: a flow formerly
counted under test_sourced can now appear under a sibling key. WHICH flows are
excluded does not change -- the population is defined by the same function --
only what they are called.

